qmapanything-token-quant demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/qmapanything-token-quant/) is a CPU-only clear-experiment
toy inspired by:

  He, Zhang, Zhang, Sui, See, Boukhers, and Yang,
  "Rotation Is Token-Blind: A Structural Criterion for Post-Training
  Quantization of Feed-Forward Geometry Transformers",
  arXiv:2611.07955 (November 2026)
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.07955
  https://arxiv.org/html/2611.07955

The reproducibility statement says code and configuration files will be
released upon acceptance. No QMapAnything repository was found on 2026-11-10.
The host model MapAnything lives at
https://github.com/facebookresearch/map-anything (Apache-2.0) and is not
vendored and not executed. This app does not download weights.

Found via a bookmarked X post by @vincieye:
  https://x.com/vincieye/status/2119415188013138070
That post was not fetched. The claim was checked on the arXiv HTML.

The Hadamard transform and symmetric absmax quantizer implemented here are
classical. QuaRot (Ashkboos et al., 2024) is cited by the paper as the
rotation baseline and is not vendored.

No warranty. Research / demo use.
